WEBVTT

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:05.480
<i>The castle town Utsunomiya,
in Tochigi Prefecture.</i>

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.610
<b>Nihonbashi</b>

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:10.150
<b>Koushu Kaidou</b>

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:15.450
<b>Nakasendou</b>

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:15.450
<b>Utsunomiya</b>

00:00:06.070 --> 00:00:10.230
<i>The Ouukaidou and Nikko Kaidou of the 
Edo Five Routes once ran through</i>

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:15.450
<b>Nikko</b>

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:15.450
<b>Nikko Kaidou</b>

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:15.450
<i>seventeen post towns,
 splitting toward Ouu and Nikko.</i>

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:15.450
<b>Shirakawa</b>

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:15.450
<b>Ouukaidou</b>

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:19.950
<i>Modern-day international tourist destinations 
such as Nikko Toushougu Shrine,</i>

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.710
<i>Lake Chuzenji, Kegon Falls,</i>

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:27.860
<i>and countless hot springs can be 
found in Nikko National Park.</i>

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:32.440
<i>With the Nikko volcano range to the north,</i>

00:00:33.670 --> 00:00:36.130
<i>the course entrance is buzzing with activity.</i>

00:00:38.120 --> 00:00:45.330
<i>It is here in Utsunomiya, where the
Tochigi Inter-High Road Race will start.</i>

00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:57.300
It's starting.

00:00:58.940 --> 00:01:02.830
The scorching three-day race 
that is the Inter-High.

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.270
<b><i>Yowamushi Pedal</i></b>

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:38.590
It's nearly time. It's nearly time.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.030
<i>RIDE.16  The Second Inter-High</i>

00:02:38.590 --> 00:02:41.640
The real race starts now, guys!

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:45.640
The training camp and our 
practices were all for this day.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:51.350
We won't be riding the day of the Inter-High,
but our team can't ride without us.

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:53.360
Hold your heads high, first-years.

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:55.080
We are the team's support.

00:02:55.080 --> 00:02:58.960
Yes, we are the seventh member 
of the Inter-High team.

00:02:58.960 --> 00:02:59.740
Yes, sir.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:03.280
Ask me if you have any questions.
Ask me anything.

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:04.330
Yes, sir.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:08.540
That's right. After all, I was 
at the Inter-High last year.

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.790
<i>My brother's so cool.</i>

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:15.270
That happy guy is really taking charge.

00:03:15.270 --> 00:03:19.670
Yeah. Since Sugimoto-kun's a hard worker,
the first-years listen to him.

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:22.780
The bicycle team is pumped.

00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:24.530
After all, they're going to the Inter-High.

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.390
Hey.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:30.850
T-Tachibana-san?

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.360
You're Kanzaki-san's friend.

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.540
What are you doing here?

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:34.820
Took you long enough to notice.

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.110
You finally remembered my name, huh?

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.110
S-Sorry.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:41.370
The tennis club lost in the 
Inter-High qualifier.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:43.120
I didn't have any plans for summer break,

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.250
so I emailed Miki to say I was 
thinking about coming to cheer on the

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:47.440
bicycle club again this year.

00:03:47.440 --> 00:03:50.460
"Want to take the bus with us this year?"

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.460
And she invited me along.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.350
I got Teshima-senpai's permission.

00:03:54.350 --> 00:03:55.020
Really?

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:57.600
You'll be working hard to earn your place.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.630
Yikes, you're strict.

00:03:59.630 --> 00:04:04.760
Anyway, I thought I'd watch you ride again.

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:05.640
What?

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:09.060
It's hot, but good luck.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:11.150
G-Good...

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.520
You told him exactly how you felt, Aya-chan.

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.250
D-Don't say it like that.

00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:17.200
He'll think it means something.

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.100
Stop smiling. Stop clapping.

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.690
Onoda-kun doesn't know how to react.

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:23.340
We're here.

00:04:23.340 --> 00:04:23.900
Huh?

00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:31.580
<b>Inter-High Road Race</b>

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:35.620
Let's go over there.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:38.580
I heard it's already over 25 degrees,
and it's still morning!

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:40.250
It's so hot.

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:44.840
Are they the press?

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:46.180
Wow.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:49.120
Seriously? Whoa.

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.310
Hey, what's their problem?

00:04:49.640 --> 00:04:51.310
<b>Kanagawa Prefecture</b>

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:54.940
That bus is huge.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.900
Hakone Academy High School.

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:09.590
They're coming out.

00:05:09.590 --> 00:05:10.410
They're here.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:13.660
The absolute champions, 
Hakone Academy High School!

00:05:13.660 --> 00:05:16.090
Their captain, Izumida, grew his hair out.

00:05:16.090 --> 00:05:18.000
They're so intense.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:19.350
Look this way, please.

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.340
Ashikiba's huge.

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.670
It's Kuroda.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:24.770
He swept the newbie races as a first-year.

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:27.940
There's more press here than we expected.

00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:32.100
Who said there wouldn't be so many since 
we placed second last year, Touichirou?

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:35.100
It's the champion's destiny, Yuki.

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.150
I'm Doubashi. Take pictures of me.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:41.150
I'm Hakone Academy High School's
next fastest man.

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:42.320
Yuki-chan.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:43.050
What's up?

00:05:43.470 --> 00:05:45.390
I forgot my charger again.

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:46.400
Forget it.

00:05:47.780 --> 00:05:49.410
Manami-kun!

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:52.870
He looked this way!

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:54.580
Hold that pose!

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:55.180
You're popular, Manami.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:57.590
I wonder why.

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:58.880
Huh?

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:02.500
One, two, three... One's missing.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.170
We're finally here.

00:06:10.810 --> 00:06:13.470
Wait up, reporters!

00:06:15.640 --> 00:06:18.890
Izumida-kun, could you look this way again?

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.280
Hey, come on. We're the 
ones who won last year.

00:06:22.280 --> 00:06:27.570
Come and get us. Have you forgotten 
last year's fierce battle?

00:06:27.570 --> 00:06:29.470
Sohoku High School's right here.

00:06:29.470 --> 00:06:31.500
The flashiest man around is right here.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.620
Who cares about
 Hakone Academy High School? Hey!

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:36.550
We won last year, right?

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.830
Uh, yeah.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:40.940
Aya-chan, weren't you watching?

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:42.710
I knew it.

00:06:42.710 --> 00:06:45.290
That's just how it is, Naruko.

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:48.800
The press's actions tell us exactly 
what everyone thinks of us.

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:50.710
I know.

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:53.010
Bring it on.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.680
In other words, we don't stand out enough.

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:01.040
Anytime you reach great heights,
people always say the first time is a fluke.

00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:03.620
You have to win twice before 
they'll acknowledge you.

00:07:04.360 --> 00:07:07.980
We can do it. I'll support 
you with all my might.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:13.450
Let's win again this year.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:14.700
Yeah!

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.870
Murakami, the wheels go over there.

00:07:20.870 --> 00:07:21.170
Okay.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.290
I told you to tidy up the 
upperclassmen's shoes.

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:25.840
All the teams are here.

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:28.890
There are tons of teams. They're raring to go.

00:07:28.890 --> 00:07:30.260
I expect no less from the Inter-High.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.890
Teams from all over the country are here.

00:07:33.710 --> 00:07:34.850
The entire country...

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:39.480
They've put their lives on the line 
for this day, for just three days.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:41.010
Of course they have.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:45.810
All their hopes from the past 
year are riding on this race.

00:07:47.310 --> 00:07:48.280
Oh, right. Teshima-san...

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:49.400
What is it?

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:54.410
After we check in and get our number tags,
I need to disappear to take care of something.

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:55.530
Something?

00:07:57.420 --> 00:07:59.160
Just some minor business.

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:10.460
<b>Chiba
Sohoku High School</b>

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:03.750
<i>I'm nervous.</i>

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:07.170
<i>No, wait. Kaburagi-kun must 
be more nervous than me.</i>

00:08:07.170 --> 00:08:10.460
<i>I should smile and talk 
to him like a real senior.</i>

00:08:10.460 --> 00:08:15.230
K-Kaburagi-kun, aren't you nervous?
Last year, I...

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:19.520
Huh? Kaburagi-kun's not here.

00:08:19.520 --> 00:08:24.340
You mean the showoff?
He's off at the usual place.

00:08:24.340 --> 00:08:27.190
Aw, crap...

00:08:30.110 --> 00:08:35.860
<b>Kanagawa
Hakone Academy High School</b>

00:08:30.790 --> 00:08:32.870
Wow, that's new.

00:08:32.870 --> 00:08:34.740
Of course.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:38.050
This year's are assigned 
based on last year's results.

00:08:38.050 --> 00:08:40.570
The perennial champions, Hakone Academy...

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:43.320
...are wearing two-digit tags.

00:08:49.090 --> 00:08:51.280
Make sure they're secured with safety pins.

00:08:51.280 --> 00:08:52.050
Got it.

00:08:52.750 --> 00:08:53.320
Onoda!

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.080
Yes, sir.

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:57.250
What?

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:02.970
What do you think of this?

00:09:02.970 --> 00:09:05.560
I knew these were coming, but just 
look at these single-digit tags!

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.000
I'm super hyped now!

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:09.690
Take a picture of me, manager.

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:12.370
Get a real good shot.

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:13.320
Okay.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:14.880
This is seriously awesome.

00:09:13.570 --> 00:09:15.150
They're so excited.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.510
Look, hotshot. Single digits.

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:18.420
Are single-digit tags that big a deal?

00:09:16.510 --> 00:09:17.700
Shut up. I know.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:18.420
I have one, too.

00:09:18.420 --> 00:09:19.910
Yeah. Look.

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.890
The other teams have
two or three-digit tags.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:23.660
You're right.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.090
The number on the left represents 
their approximate rank last year.

00:09:27.090 --> 00:09:31.190
The single digit tags 
mean they won last year.

00:09:31.190 --> 00:09:32.170
Huh.

00:09:32.590 --> 00:09:35.530
The number on the right is 
their rank within their team.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:38.970
Since each team has six riders, 
they range from one to six.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:43.820
One is a special number. 
It's the ace's number.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:45.550
Cycling is interesting.

00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:46.890
Isn't it?

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.220
Um, Teshima-san...

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.270
This tag...

00:09:51.780 --> 00:09:54.480
Why not? I think it looks good on you.

00:09:54.830 --> 00:09:57.560
But isn't this Imaizumi-kun's?

00:09:58.230 --> 00:09:59.070
Huh?

00:09:59.930 --> 00:10:01.910
Every race is the same.

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:06.160
When the previous winner rides again,
he's given that tag.

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:08.460
It's a symbol of victory.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:10.330
The #1 tag.

00:10:14.990 --> 00:10:16.780
It's a symbol of victory.

00:10:16.780 --> 00:10:18.140
The #1 tag.

00:10:20.790 --> 00:10:23.760
I'm... #1.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:28.230
If last year's winner was a third-year who's
since graduated, its meaning may be different.

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:30.270
Good.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:35.560
You earned that number when Kinjou-san, 
Tadokoro-san, Makishima-san,

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:38.280
Naruko, and I entrusted 
you with our hopes last year,

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:41.750
and you took them to the finish line.

00:10:43.800 --> 00:10:45.370
Imaizumi-kun...

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:50.380
Onoda, you'll be carrying 
all our hopes as you ride.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.130
Hold your head high.

00:10:58.370 --> 00:10:59.420
Got it.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:03.940
Kaburagi's still not back.

00:11:03.940 --> 00:11:04.760
Where's Naruko?

00:11:05.090 --> 00:11:06.770
He just headed that way.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:10.310
Come to think of it, didn't he say he 
had some minor business to take care of?

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:14.360
<b>Kyoto
Kyoto Fushimi High School</b>

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:14.360
Excuse me for a second.

00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:17.400
Who the hell are you?

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.360
Don't mind me.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:21.990
It's been a while.

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:24.800
Haven't seen you since 
last winter, Midousuji.

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:31.460
Well, well, well, well, well, well, well...

00:11:31.460 --> 00:11:35.230
If it isn't Chiba's redhead.

00:11:35.230 --> 00:11:37.420
What are you doing here? 
Cheering us on?

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:39.960
I'm here to race on my bike.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:42.430
Hey, this is the
Kyoto Fushimi High School tent!

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:45.260
I, Captain Mizuta, will deal 
with any outsiders who—

00:11:46.360 --> 00:11:52.690
I thought you quit sprinting 
after losing to me.

00:11:52.690 --> 00:11:55.790
So why are you still riding your bike?

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:59.460
I love my bike and my friends above all else.

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:01.240
That's the kind of man Naruko Shoukichi is.

00:12:03.220 --> 00:12:04.310
Nonsense.

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:08.030
Friends? Race?

00:12:08.740 --> 00:12:10.540
Race who?

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.120
You, Idiotsuji.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:16.460
<i>He's not backing down from 
Midousuji-kun's pressure.</i>

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:19.420
<i>They raced each other in Osaka a while back.</i>

00:12:19.960 --> 00:12:23.950
<i>Midousuji-kun's pressure has been so 
great lately, even I recoil from him,</i>

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:27.090
<i>and we're on the same team.</i>

00:12:27.680 --> 00:12:30.550
We can't promise that! Get out of—

00:12:30.550 --> 00:12:31.740
Sure.

00:12:31.740 --> 00:12:33.060
Midousuji-kun?

00:12:33.060 --> 00:12:37.820
After all, you're the one who made me fly.

00:12:38.800 --> 00:12:41.910
I'll race you.

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:45.770
However, you'll only get 
one chance.

00:12:45.770 --> 00:12:48.140
Don't miss it.

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:50.440
That's plenty. Thanks.

00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:51.620
Later.

00:12:54.100 --> 00:12:56.990
Oh, right. Let me tell you something.

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:58.960
If you're thinking about 
pulling ahead of me on a climb,

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:00.850
since I'm stronger on the flats,

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:02.050
don't waste your time.

00:13:03.110 --> 00:13:04.550
This year...

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:08.220
I switched to being an all-rounder.

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:10.410
What?

00:13:10.410 --> 00:13:11.470
See you later.

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:15.900
<i>Rooster head's an all-rounder?</i>

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:19.980
<i>That gives me a good idea.</i>

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:22.600
<i>The opening ceremony will begin shortly.</i>

00:13:22.600 --> 00:13:25.240
<i>All participants,
please gather around the stage.</i>

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.350
Crap! I can't do it!
I can't hold it in anymore!

00:13:27.350 --> 00:13:28.960
I'm going to poop my pants!

00:13:28.960 --> 00:13:32.910
Oh, come on! Why does my stomach 
have to do this at the Inter-High?

00:13:32.910 --> 00:13:35.440
I can't hold it anymore! Hurry up!

00:13:37.110 --> 00:13:38.370
It's open.

00:13:39.570 --> 00:13:43.240
Quit banging on the door!

00:13:43.240 --> 00:13:44.090
Huh?

00:13:44.400 --> 00:13:47.660
I hope you knew you were 
banging on the door of

00:13:47.660 --> 00:13:50.720
Hakone Academy's
next fastest man, Doubashi-sama!

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:53.080
Crap, it's Doubashi.

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:53.920
From Hakone?

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:54.850
Let's go.

00:13:53.920 --> 00:13:55.600
Hey, you!

00:13:54.850 --> 00:13:55.600
Y-Yeah.

00:13:55.600 --> 00:13:56.730
What?

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:59.480
I'm talking to you, orange head!

00:14:02.230 --> 00:14:04.860
Let me take a dump first!

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:15.450
Okay, now let's talk.

00:14:15.450 --> 00:14:18.040
Quit sparkling! You've got some nerve!

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:22.360
You were shouting at me while you 
knocked on my door, weren't you?

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.760
Sorry about that.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:32.180
Before every race, I go someplace 
isolated to focus myself.

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:33.200
But you...

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.470
Come out! Just come out already!

00:14:34.470 --> 00:14:35.240
One more second!

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:36.840
I'll hate you forever! I'll curse you to death!

00:14:36.840 --> 00:14:37.600
Just come out!

00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:40.020
Come out already, you pig!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:43.420
You distracted me! Who are 
you calling a pig, huh?

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:48.310
Sorry. I was having an emergency, 
so I let that slip out.

00:14:48.310 --> 00:14:51.360
Slip out, my ass! How did 
your parents raise you?

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:52.370
What?

00:14:55.050 --> 00:14:57.950
That jersey...
You're from Sohoku High School.

00:14:57.950 --> 00:14:59.370
You're a Chiba country bumpkin.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:00.500
What?

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:04.630
Don't let your lucky 
victory go to your head.

00:15:05.020 --> 00:15:07.050
You wanna fight, huh?

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:10.260
<i>He's fast.</i>

00:15:10.690 --> 00:15:13.380
<i>He reacted the moment I reached out my hand.</i>

00:15:14.840 --> 00:15:17.470
<i>He's fast, even though he's big.</i>

00:15:17.850 --> 00:15:21.310
<i>I haven't seen this orange head
 on Sohoku's team before.</i>

00:15:21.310 --> 00:15:24.230
<i>He must be a first-year. He's got some nerve.</i>

00:15:24.640 --> 00:15:27.730
<i>He hasn't taken a step back, 
even though I grabbed him.</i>

00:15:28.180 --> 00:15:30.790
It wasn't luck that Sohoku High School won.

00:15:30.790 --> 00:15:32.110
Take it back, pig.

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.970
How could it have been anything but luck

00:15:34.970 --> 00:15:40.120
that let your skinny Onoda 
kid win at the very end?

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:41.750
Onoda-san is strong!

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.380
You just think he's strong!

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:44.930
What?

00:15:44.930 --> 00:15:46.950
There are two types of truth.

00:15:46.950 --> 00:15:51.090
The real truth, and the lie that 
people are convinced is the truth.

00:15:51.090 --> 00:15:52.630
He's the latter.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.390
He's wearing a crown he 
won through sheer luck,

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:57.390
but everyone's too scared 
to doing anything about it.

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:57.970
You're wrong!

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:00.390
Have you ever tested him?

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.100
Have you ever really raced him?

00:16:03.440 --> 00:16:05.680
He disguises himself as 
an Inter-High champion.

00:16:05.680 --> 00:16:08.790
Everyone fawns over him 
and thinks he's amazing.

00:16:09.580 --> 00:16:11.360
Is he actually strong?

00:16:11.360 --> 00:16:14.700
Is he stronger than everyone 
else you've ever met?

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:21.120
No, I know how he rides!

00:16:21.650 --> 00:16:24.540
I saw him on Mt. Fuji at 
last year's Inter-High!

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.170
He's the real thing!

00:16:26.740 --> 00:16:31.380
He's the reason I abandoned the other schools 
and chose to come to Sohoku High School!

00:16:31.810 --> 00:16:35.140
Are you sure you're not just viewing 
things through a self-imposed filter?

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.200
What?

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:40.140
Sohoku High School is strong. 
At least, they should be.

00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:42.310
They have to be strong.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:45.020
Otherwise, the path you've followed

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:50.070
and all your work would be meaningless.

00:16:58.730 --> 00:17:01.580
Face the truth, orange kid.

00:17:02.410 --> 00:17:05.320
Hakone Academy High School has 
the most members of any team.

00:17:05.320 --> 00:17:07.810
No one can compare to how much we practice.

00:17:08.410 --> 00:17:11.370
Who's stronger? There's only one truth.

00:17:11.370 --> 00:17:12.840
The strongest team...

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:16.550
...is us, Hakone Academy High School!

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:19.330
The strongest...

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:26.080
There's only one truth.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:29.290
<i>The strongest are chosen at the Inter-High.</i>

00:17:29.290 --> 00:17:31.310
<i>Participants are measured and screened.</i>

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:37.320
<i>This hot, long, and harsh race all 
comes down to how much you train.</i>

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:42.700
<i>Overwhelming physical and mental strength...</i>

00:17:37.550 --> 00:17:39.320
<b>Pork Roast</b>

00:17:45.250 --> 00:17:47.960
The reinstatement of Hakone Academy 
High School as the champions.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:52.700
It's what we must do one week 
from now at the Inter-High.

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.630
There's no need to let any 
threats stay in the race.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:18:00.050
Keep a close eye on them and push them out.

00:18:00.760 --> 00:18:02.430
There's no need to hold back.

00:18:02.430 --> 00:18:06.950
Push them out, huh? Sure, I'll do it.

00:18:06.950 --> 00:18:11.150
In the name of Hakone Academy 
High School, I'll do it.

00:18:11.150 --> 00:18:15.020
<i>How many can I get on the first day?</i>

00:18:17.530 --> 00:18:20.490
He's back. Kaburagi-kun!

00:18:21.610 --> 00:18:22.660
<i>Onoda-san...</i>

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:24.780
Is your stomach okay?

00:18:24.780 --> 00:18:28.290
You should warm up a little bit.

00:18:28.840 --> 00:18:30.280
<i>This guy...</i>

00:18:31.130 --> 00:18:32.500
Do you want to take some medicine?

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:34.100
The race is starting soon.

00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:36.500
The opening ceremony is being 
held at the stage over there.

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:39.010
Should I go get you some medicine?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:40.340
Onoda-kun!

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:41.930
What are you doing?

00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:43.370
Sorry, sorry.

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:45.070
Are you okay?

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:47.770
<i>Is this guy actually strong?</i>

00:18:45.070 --> 00:18:46.210
Here, I'll help.

00:18:46.210 --> 00:18:47.770
Th-Thanks, Naruko-kun.

00:18:50.060 --> 00:18:55.030
Welcome last year's champions, representing 
Chiba prefecture, Sohoku High School.

00:18:56.130 --> 00:18:58.480
Th-The cheers are so loud.

00:18:58.480 --> 00:19:00.620
Winning really is amazing.

00:19:00.620 --> 00:19:02.330
They're going onstage.

00:19:02.330 --> 00:19:04.320
Isn't it cool, Danchiku-kun?

00:19:04.320 --> 00:19:05.290
Yeah.

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:09.990
Captaining the team this year 
is third-year Teshima Junta.

00:19:11.730 --> 00:19:15.730
Then we have another third-year,
 sprinter Aoyagi Hajime.

00:19:17.040 --> 00:19:22.890
Acting as the team's ace this year 
is second-year Imaizumi Shunsuke.

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:26.510
<b>Ima</b>

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:26.510
<b>izumi</b>

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:25.430
Imaizumi-kun!

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.510
He's so cool!

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:26.510
He said he's the ace.

00:19:26.910 --> 00:19:31.220
And another second-year, the Man 
of Red Flames, Naruko Shoukichi.

00:19:33.470 --> 00:19:34.660
It's the red guy!

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:35.820
Heat up the race!

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:37.030
Stand out again this year!

00:19:37.470 --> 00:19:39.960
All your fans are dudes.

00:19:39.960 --> 00:19:42.320
Shut up! What's wrong with that?

00:19:42.700 --> 00:19:44.990
Let's not forget about this man.

00:19:46.710 --> 00:19:49.850
Last year's general classification 
Inter-High champion.

00:19:49.850 --> 00:19:53.040
Despite being new to road racing, 
he climbed all the way to the top.

00:19:53.040 --> 00:19:54.420
Bearer of number tag #1.

00:19:54.420 --> 00:19:58.090
The little climber, Onoda Sakamichi.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:03.770
Your dramatic riding during the final stage 
of last year's third day was fantastic.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:04.890
Could you give us a few words?

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:08.930
What? Uh, um... h-hello...

00:20:08.930 --> 00:20:11.110
I'm Onyoda Chakamichi!

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:14.030
<i>I...</i>

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:16.990
What are your goals for this year?

00:20:16.990 --> 00:20:18.780
Th-This year?

00:20:19.250 --> 00:20:21.350
This year I've been going 
to Akiba every Thursday...

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:24.030
Onoda-kun, the audience already loves you!

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:29.040
<i>It's true that I didn't see 
all of last year's race.</i>

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:27.200
I meant your goals for the race.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.620
Oh, my goals.

00:20:29.620 --> 00:20:30.820
Well, I...

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.540
You don't need to hold the mic.

00:20:32.900 --> 00:20:38.290
<i>I didn't actually see how he 
rode during the Inter-High.</i>

00:20:38.290 --> 00:20:42.800
I'll do my best, and... yeah, 
I'll do my best at the end.

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:41.720
<i>Is he actually strong?</i>

00:20:44.590 --> 00:20:46.750
Oh, uh, is that enough?

00:20:46.750 --> 00:20:47.800
<i>Is this team...</i>

00:20:47.090 --> 00:20:51.350
Finally, there's first-year Kaburagi Issa.

00:20:51.350 --> 00:20:53.810
<i>...actually strong?</i>

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:57.680
<i>I've trained harder than everyone else.</i>

00:20:57.680 --> 00:20:59.320
<i>I'll knock them aside.</i>

00:20:59.710 --> 00:21:01.320
<i>It'll be easy.</i>

00:21:01.690 --> 00:21:05.450
You're doing well, Doubashi, 
but don't go too hard.

00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.800
Our mechanic was crying about it.

00:21:08.280 --> 00:21:10.230
I heard you bent another one out of shape,

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:13.060
even though he just swapped it out yesterday.

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:16.570
The handlebars were too weak.

00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:18.670
They can't withstand the 
power of my sprinting.

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:21.710
He's only on rollers,
but he's still intimidating.

00:21:21.710 --> 00:21:26.720
I heard he's won all the sprint races 
he's participated in this year.

00:21:26.720 --> 00:21:29.300
Yeah, apparently it's unprecedented.

00:21:29.300 --> 00:21:32.200
They call him the Monster of the Road.

00:21:32.770 --> 00:21:34.960
Road Monster Doubashi!

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:40.060
No one stands a chance against me!

00:23:12.660 --> 00:23:14.240
He looked this way!

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:15.230
Hold that pose!

00:23:15.230 --> 00:23:17.340
He sure does have a lot of fans.

00:23:17.860 --> 00:23:20.150
He might have more than 
Toudou-san did last year.

00:23:20.150 --> 00:23:22.580
Manami, make them shut up!

00:23:22.580 --> 00:23:24.060
I can't focus!

00:23:24.060 --> 00:23:25.200
What?

00:23:25.670 --> 00:23:26.250
Oh.

00:23:32.170 --> 00:23:34.300
Why did you make them louder?

00:23:36.410 --> 00:23:39.930
<i>NEXT RIDE  Start!!!</i>

00:23:39.930 --> 00:23:44.940
This is a work of fiction. All characters and organizations
 appearing in this work are fictional. In this work,
 characters sometimes engage in dangerous activities.
 While riding bicycles on actual roads,
 please follow all traffic laws and ride safely.

00:23:44.940 --> 00:23:51.000
<b><i>The high cadence
 continues!!</i></b>
